Solidification, partitioning, segregation and morphological stability (@mat-solidification: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Phases-and-Diffusion-DoITPoMS.lingua#r_4HHCB32507KCQ5FPHGT4JD5GTB", #source "../sources/Kinetic-Processes-in-Materials-MIT.lingua#r_2BZVQ9NG9Y2XTF4QG0H3JYYS16", #source "../sources/Termodinamica-dos-Materiais-Cota.lingua#r_05ES8F38ASNQEQMZ0HY6709Z0Z", #materials-engineering "Spinodal-decomposition-gradient-energy-and-conserved-fields.lingua#r_4HB6D1YCX2GC5GYD33G1140PY4") { r_5CHRBTJKPKKJQ5V4WDW12GGV78
**Read:** [Phases, diffusion and solidification — Cambridge DoITPoMS](../sources/Phases-and-Diffusion-DoITPoMS.lingua#r_4HHCB32507KCQ5FPHGT4JD5GTB), the entire Solidification of Alloys package; [Materials kinetics — MIT 3.205 and 3.21](../sources/Kinetic-Processes-in-Materials-MIT.lingua#r_2BZVQ9NG9Y2XTF4QG0H3JYYS16), 3.205 lectures 8–9; [Termodinâmica dos Materiais — Cota, 2026](../sources/Termodinamica-dos-Materiais-Cota.lingua#r_05ES8F38ASNQEQMZ0HY6709Z0Z), binary and ternary solidification examples.

Local partitioning and transport shape the final solid. Under complete liquid mixing, negligible solid diffusion, local interfacial equilibrium and constant partition coefficient k, the Scheil model gives c_L=c_0(1−f_s)^(k−1), with newly formed solid c_S=kc_L. It does not give the mean composition of all solid as kc_L.

For illustrative c_0=0.05, k=0.5 and f_s=0.75, c_L=0.10, the new solid has c_S=0.05, and the accumulated solid's mean is (0.05−0.25×0.10)/0.75=1/30. Real terminal reactions or changing partition behavior prevent extending a divergent formula indefinitely.

**Work:** Derive the liquid balance and distinguish equilibrium cooling from the Scheil limit. Relate thermal and solute gradients to planar-interface stability and dendrites. Compare a microsegregation prediction with spatial chemical measurements and explain what later homogenization could change.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
